{\pard\f0\fs15\li576\fi-576\tx576 A\tab 1. According to John, chapter 3, verse 1, of what was Nicodemus a member?\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576 A. The Jewish ruling council (John 3:1)\par}
{\pard\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576\fi-576\tx576 X\tab 2. In John, chapter 3, whom did Nicodemus know was a teacher who had come from God?\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576 A. Jesus (John 3:2)\par}
{\pard\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576\fi-576\tx576 S\tab 3. Situation question: who said it, and to whom: "Rabbi, we know that you are a teacher who has come from God. For no one could perform the signs you are doing if God were not with him."?\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576 A. Nicodemus said it to Jesus (John 3:2)\par}
{\pard\par}
{\pard\f0\fs15\li576\fi-576\tx576 G\tab 4. To whom did Nicodemus come at night?\par}
